1
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:51,940
[Mystic Nine]
[Adapted from the novel of Kennedy Xu]

2
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,980
[Episode 19]
[This story is purely fictional]

3
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,610
Where are the pouches Jiu gave us?

4
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:52,780
It's not time yet.

5
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:53,940
We can't open them.

6
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:57,450
Jiu

7
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,410
guards against us like we're thieves.

8
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:04,580
[Private Room One]

9
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:21,540
President Tottori, what an honor

10
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:23,010
to meet you today.

11
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:43,290
Chief Editor Liang.

12
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:47,340
Have you

13
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,380
set your sights on any lots today?

14
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,540
President Tottori,

15
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,100
greetings.

16
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:56,730
I'm Chen Minzhi, Deputy Chief Editor

17
00:03:57,150 --> 00:03:57,890
of Yahe Monthly.

18
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,060
I've heard so much

19
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,340
about you.

20
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:03,940
With you here at today's auction,

21
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:05,610
Chief Editor Liang and I

22
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,170
feel much more assured.

23
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,380
If you have any instructions,

24
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:10,540
just say the word.

25
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,450
We'll do everything in our power

26
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,540
and won't be

27
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,540
the slightest bit remiss.

28
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:19,700
Yahe Monthly

29
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,020
certainly has no shortage of talent.

30
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:27,490
Editor Chen

31
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,340
has devoted himself fully

32
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,660
to our magazine.

33
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,370
Since he rarely gets to come here,

34
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,610
I brought him to broaden his horizons.

35
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:35,580
By the way, sir,

36
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,900
what are your plans for tonight?

37
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,250
I hope you won't take offense.

38
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:43,540
But this time,

39
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,730
I've brought another expert,

40
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,850
so my funds will have to be split between you.

41
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,780
If someone is more qualified than I am,

42
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:51,900
I'll gladly step aside.

43
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:52,610
Good.

44
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:53,900
Come.

45
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:55,540
Allow me to introduce you.

46
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:57,050
This

47
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,220
is the adviser I've invited:

48
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:02,610
Seventh Madam of the Mystic Nine,

49
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,250
Miss Huo.

50
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:09,980
Chief Editor Liang,

51
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:11,410
a pleasure.

52
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,850
You bear some resemblance

53
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,580
to an old friend of mine.

54
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,460
Then we must be destined to meet.

55
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:23,460
All right.

56
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,390
The auction is about to begin.

57
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,780
Let me explain tonight's plan.

58
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,850
I don't want our two private rooms

59
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,700
competing directly

60
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,290
and driving up each other's bids.

61
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,100
That would benefit none of us.

62
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:38,140
So,

63
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,580
whenever we bid on an item,

64
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,700
Chief Editor Liang, please don't bid.

65
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:44,540
Understood.

66
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:46,540
If we don't pursue a lot,

67
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,340
you may use your own judgment

68
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:51,370
and bid as you please.

69
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,930
Look at the curtain outside our room.

70
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
If a bouquet is pinned to it,

71
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,290
that means we want the lot.

72
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:00,700
If there isn't one,

73
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,810
it's yours to pursue.

74
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:04,810
Rest assured.

75
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:05,810
We won't

76
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:06,900
disrupt your plans, sir.

77
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,050
I look forward to working with you.

78
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:10,810
Likewise.

79
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:16,020
We'll take our leave.

80
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,140
What is it?

81
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,980
Something about those two feels off.

82
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:37,220
Instead of editors, they seem

83
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:38,700
more like military officers.

84
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,290
Once we see

85
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,220
how they act at the auction,

86
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:43,050
we'll know, won't we?

87
00:06:56,270 --> 00:06:57,370
Xiangu came here

88
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,730
but didn't expose us.

89
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,220
She must be here for Laogou.

90
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,980
She'll probably help us.

91
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,780
My concern is that besides Laogou,

92
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,340
she may have more complicated motives.

93
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:11,250
We can only adapt as things unfold.

94
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:13,980
I trust the Mystic Nine know where to draw the line.

95
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,100
Most of the Mystic Nine

96
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:16,850
are here at Xinyue Restaurant.

97
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,730
If something goes wrong,

98
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,900
only two of the Mystic Nine will remain.

99
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,220
Let's hope Chen Pi and Heibei behave themselves.

100
00:07:30,430 --> 00:07:31,370
It's about time.

101
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,760
Take out the pouches.

102
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:40,370
Give them to me.

103
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:41,850
Jiu said to read

104
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,170
the one with the large patterns first.

105
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,020
What a nuisance.

106
00:07:55,750 --> 00:07:56,660
Can you even read it?

107
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:02,500
[The key to securing what you want at an auction]

108
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,800
[is whether anyone else]

109
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,100
[wants the same item.]

110
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:09,490
At Xinyue Restaurant auctions,

111
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:10,540
most guests

112
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,980
don't come with a particular item in mind.

113
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:15,220
They're mostly wealthy people hunting for treasures.

114
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,050
Before the artifact chests come up,

115
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:19,540
we need someone

116
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,540
to drive up the price of every earlier lot.

117
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,890
Distinguished guests,

118
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,670
the early session of the auction

119
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:36,010
is about to begin.

120
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,100
All unauthorized persons must leave.

121
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,340
During the auction,

122
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,370
please remain silent.

123
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:47,700
We will now present the lots.

124
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:51,100
The minimum bid increment is 5,000.

125
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,530
Here is today's first lot.

126
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:59,610
Isn't that a piece of Song Jun ware?

127
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,240
Jun ware is said to rival jade

128
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,660
and even surpass it in beauty.

129
00:09:04,030 --> 00:09:05,250
That rose-purple glaze

130
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,600
is truly rare.

131
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:12,110
Rare? What is this rubbish?

132
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,580
A rose-red glazed apple-form vase.

133
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:18,250
Its purple glaze is like clouds at dusk,

134
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:19,770
its glow like the morning sky.

135
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,650
It is among the finest surviving Song Jun pieces.

136
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:29,820
Miss Huo,

137
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:32,420
what do you think of this lot?

138
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,530
The glaze is beautiful,

139
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,370
but it was poorly fired.

140
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,530
It certainly is no ordinary piece.

141
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,730
Bidding begins!

142
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:49,300
Ten thousand.

143
00:09:49,510 --> 00:09:51,980
Table 11 bids 10,000.

144
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:53,820
Sixty thousand.

145
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,060
Private Room Six bids 60,000!

146
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:06,650
That's why we need two teams here.

147
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,180
Chen Pi and Heibei,

148
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,340
your task

149
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:11,370
is to drive up the price of every lot.

150
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,850
Everyone wants to enter the late session.

151
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,100
They must spend enough...

152
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:17,890
- Seventy thousand. - to win three lots.

153
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,530
You need to make them believe...

154
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,130
A hundred thousand.

155
00:10:20,150 --> 00:10:22,100
that entering tonight's late session will be difficult.

156
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:23,890
Private Room Six bids 100,000!

157
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,300
Any higher bids?

158
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,300
Should we go higher?

159
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:39,770
A hundred and five thousand!

160
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:44,130
Table 11 bids 105,000.

161
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:48,460
A hundred and five thousand, going once.

162
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,530
A hundred and five thousand, going twice.

163
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:55,890
A hundred and five thousand, third and final call.

164
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:58,700
Sold!

165
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:00,530
Congratulations to this guest

166
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:02,700
on winning today's first lot.

167
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,980
Let us congratulate our distinguished guests at Table 11!

168
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:08,780
Congratulations.

169
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,090
At such a high price.

170
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,700
That wasn't difficult.

171
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:23,940
Driving up the price isn't difficult.

172
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,850
But Xinyue Restaurant is highly experienced.

173
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,490
After we do this a few times,

174
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:31,460
the other bidders and the restaurant

175
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:33,980
will suspect we're planted bidders

176
00:11:34,030 --> 00:11:35,060
deliberately inflating prices.

177
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,820
Then no one will follow our bids,

178
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,250
and we'll be stuck paying for the lots ourselves.

179
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:39,730
Didn't Jiu say

180
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,650
we don't need to enter the late session?

181
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:43,940
We just need to drain

182
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:45,580
everyone else's money, don't we?

183
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,250
I'll handle the next one.

184
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:48,300
You...

185
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:50,940
You didn't understand what I said at all.

186
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,530
By the final stretch of the early session,

187
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:07,370
you'll have drained everyone's funds.

188
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,700
To conserve their money,

189
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,220
no one will follow your bids.

190
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,940
Master Zhang can then secure the final three lots

191
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:15,610
at relatively low prices

192
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,940
and keep more funds in reserve.

193
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:22,140
[Beiping Branch of the Military Affairs Commission]

194
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,700
Ladies and gentlemen,

195
00:12:29,390 --> 00:12:30,730
the early session has concluded.

196
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:33,300
Those who have won three treasures,

197
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:34,820
please rest for a while.

198
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:36,530
After the Zi hour,
[*Zi hour: 11 PM to 1 AM]

199
00:12:36,530 --> 00:12:38,340
the late session will begin.

200
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:41,700
All other guests, please leave at once.

201
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:54,420
That private room kept driving up the prices.

202
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,420
They seemed to be helping...

203
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:57,300
I need to freshen up.

204
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:03,060
[Private Room One]

205
00:13:05,630 --> 00:13:06,610
Get a telephone ready for me.

206
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:07,100
Yes.

207
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:09,010
There's something wrong with Liang Bencai.

208
00:13:17,910 --> 00:13:20,010
The prices today were outrageously high.

209
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:21,300
What choice did we have?

210
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:23,940
Without winning three lots, we couldn't enter the late session.

211
00:13:24,670 --> 00:13:27,280
That fellow in Private Room Five got his lots cheaply.

212
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:28,370
Roast duck.

213
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,940
Flaky Yunnan ham pastries.

214
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:31,940
Braised shark fin with ginger and Sichuan pepper.

215
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:36,250
One moment, please.

216
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:40,850
Master Zhang,

217
00:13:41,390 --> 00:13:42,370
there's about one hour

218
00:13:42,390 --> 00:13:43,490
until the Zi hour.

219
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,300
During the intermission,

220
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:47,420
the guests in the private rooms will exchange toasts.

221
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:50,010
It's our chance to learn about our rivals in the late session.

222
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:54,700
We're posing as wartime collaborators.

223
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,610
Won't that make mingling difficult?

224
00:13:58,550 --> 00:13:59,980
Your identity does make it inconvenient.

225
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,420
I can handle this.

226
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:04,770
Did you bring your calling cards?

227
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:05,490
Yes.

228
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,490
Be careful.

229
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:20,100
Gentlemen,

230
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,240
this fruit platter is compliments of the restaurant.

231
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,130
Please enjoy.

232
00:14:27,510 --> 00:14:28,300
Chief Editor Liang,

233
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,340
Miss Yin says

234
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:31,850
there are several details

235
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:35,250
about tonight's auction she must discuss with you in person.

236
00:14:35,870 --> 00:14:38,060
Please join her in the reception room.

237
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,730
I'll go at once.

238
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,060
Editor Chen, I'll leave things here to you...

239
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:44,770
Go ahead.

240
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:54,770
One more thing.

241
00:14:55,510 --> 00:14:56,460
Mr. Yin has said

242
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,370
that during the intermission,

243
00:14:58,550 --> 00:15:00,010
the guests are free to mingle,

244
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:01,700
so unless something urgent arises,

245
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:02,730
there's no need to report it.

246
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,700
And don't disturb him.

247
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:05,490
Understood.

248
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,700
Hello. Where would you like to be connected?

249
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:19,610
Connect me

250
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:20,890
to Yahe Monthly.

251
00:15:22,510 --> 00:15:23,460
Certainly. One moment, please.

252
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:30,180
Sir,

253
00:15:30,790 --> 00:15:31,250
we're connected.

254
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:35,130
Hello.

255
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,600
- Hello. - Who are you calling for?

256
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,470
This is Soichi Kishimoto of the Beiping Office

257
00:15:38,670 --> 00:15:40,420
of the Eastern Cultural Affairs Association.

258
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,890
Mr. Kishimoto, what can I do for you?

259
00:15:43,510 --> 00:15:44,820
Where is Chief Editor Liang?

260
00:15:45,390 --> 00:15:47,730
He's attending the Military Affairs Commission's auction.

261
00:15:51,390 --> 00:15:52,060
May I ask

262
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:54,100
what Mr. Liang Bencai looks like?

263
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:55,650
Any distinguishing features?

264
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,650
Chief Editor Liang is fair-skinned and slim.

265
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:01,580
He's in his early thirties and wears round-framed glasses,

266
00:16:01,910 --> 00:16:02,650
with the air of a scholar.

267
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,180
He's fairly tall.

268
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:06,890
He always keeps his hair carefully combed

269
00:16:07,670 --> 00:16:08,460
and wears a long gown.

270
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,220
He looks very refined.

271
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:10,850
That's all.

272
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:24,580
All of that is useless.

273
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,340
From that description,

274
00:16:26,550 --> 00:16:28,490
we can't possibly tell whether he's Liang Bencai.

275
00:16:32,630 --> 00:16:34,250
Find someone who knows Liang Bencai

276
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:35,610
and bring him to Xinyue Restaurant.

277
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:36,820
Seat him in the main hall.

278
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:37,650
Yes.

279
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,250
Miss Huo,

280
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,660
Mr. Yin of Xinyue Restaurant

281
00:17:17,830 --> 00:17:18,770
would like to invite you for tea.

282
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:20,980
May I decline?

283
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,490
Of course.

284
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:24,700
However,

285
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:25,810
Miss Huo,

286
00:17:26,830 --> 00:17:28,290
of all the guests here today,

287
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,290
our boss has invited only you.

288
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,660
Aren't you curious why?

289
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:39,290
It'll only take as long as a cup of tea.

290
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:11,660
Mr. Yin.

291
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:13,180
Please come in.

292
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:25,300
[Mr. Yin]

293
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:30,770
Miss Huo, I've been waiting for you.

294
00:18:32,350 --> 00:18:32,730
Please sit.

295
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:46,660
You're famously elusive, Mr. Yin.

296
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,660
Yet today, you asked to see me.

297
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,090
May I ask why?

298
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:53,860
I invited you here to thank you.

299
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,570
Thanks to the information you provided,

300
00:18:56,830 --> 00:18:57,940
not long ago,

301
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,940
we acquired a collection of antiques.

302
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:01,460
The partnership between Xinyue Restaurant

303
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,660
and the Mystic Nine

304
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,900
usually involves the Mystic Nine acquiring antiques

305
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:05,380
and bringing them here for auction.

306
00:19:05,550 --> 00:19:06,900
But this time it was different.

307
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,900
You provided the leads yourself.

308
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,250
Therefore,

309
00:19:13,790 --> 00:19:14,660
this 200,000

310
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,660
is the reward you are owed.

311
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,380
Please accept it.

312
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:29,700
[Two hundred thousand yuan]

313
00:19:31,830 --> 00:19:32,770
Thank you, Mr. Yin.

314
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:34,940
Wait, Miss Huo.

315
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,140
You haven't had your tea yet.

316
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,180
I'd also like to ask

317
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,940
about Xiangxi.

318
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,140
Mr. Yin,

319
00:19:48,590 --> 00:19:50,180
you don't seem like the type to be concerned about the source of the goods.

320
00:19:51,350 --> 00:19:53,860
My daughter has ties to the Mystic Nine.

321
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:56,620
There are certain things I must know.

322
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:00,420
This matter concerns me alone.

323
00:20:01,070 --> 00:20:02,050
It has nothing to do with the Mystic Nine.

324
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:04,900
You're asking the wrong question, sir.

325
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:08,250
What exactly is in Xiangxi?

326
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,180
That's all the information I have.

327
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:15,250
The Mystic Nine plans to win those two artifact chests.

328
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:17,220
Am I right?

329
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,140
You knew about my plan all along?

330
00:20:21,310 --> 00:20:23,250
Then why didn't you stop it?

331
00:20:24,070 --> 00:20:25,220
I'm a businessman.

332
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:27,700
I'm interested only in results.

333
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:30,900
Quality goods benefit Xinyue Restaurant.

334
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,250
But right now, what I truly want to know

335
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:34,860
is

336
00:20:36,750 --> 00:20:37,900
what sort of person you are.

337
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:45,180
The person hardest to understand is often oneself.

338
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:46,770
Perhaps

339
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:51,050
none of us has ever truly understood who we are.

340
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,250
I can't tell you the whole story.

341
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:57,090
I doubt you would care anyway.

342
00:20:58,400 --> 00:20:59,420
All I can say

343
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,530
is that I did it to save someone.

344
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:06,530
Then why did you come with the Japanese?

345
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:12,420
Because this time,

346
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:15,620
I'm trying to save myself.

347
00:21:17,070 --> 00:21:18,770
It seems you and those around you

348
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:20,010
are in a great deal of trouble.

349
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,570
Even with danger on every side,

350
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:25,770
you still dared to use Xinyue Restaurant to lay your trap.

351
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:28,980
That takes courage.

352
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:34,050
I simply don't want to be

353
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,660
swept along by events anymore.

354
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,330
Then you can take control of the situation.

355
00:21:42,590 --> 00:21:43,860
I once thought so too.

356
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:47,420
I believed that if I took control of everything,

357
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:51,010
I could set it all back on the right course.

358
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,220
But what happened afterward

359
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,140
made me realize

360
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:56,570
that sometimes, the fault

361
00:21:58,510 --> 00:21:59,530
lies beyond any one person.

362
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,380
Perhaps for any person,

363
00:22:04,350 --> 00:22:05,420
the most important thing in life

364
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:07,220
is choosing the right path.

365
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:10,250
Only by following such a path

366
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:12,220
can one avoid losing oneself.

367
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:19,910
I understand

368
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:20,920
everything you just said.

369
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:25,670
Thank you.

370
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,140
Those two artifact chests

371
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:30,860
are the key, aren't they?

372
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,940
They contain only two ancient corpses.

373
00:22:38,110 --> 00:22:39,570
What do the Mystic Nine want with them?

374
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:43,250
Perhaps we won't know the reason

375
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,140
until we see them for ourselves.

376
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,570
For something this important,

377
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,050
is Zhang Qishan here?

378
00:22:49,510 --> 00:22:50,290
If he is,

379
00:22:51,110 --> 00:22:52,940
I can only go against my daughter's wishes

380
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:55,090
and have him beheaded on behalf

381
00:22:56,790 --> 00:22:57,730
of Xinyue Restaurant's shareholders

382
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:01,330
to uphold the rules.

383
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:03,490
If you truly wanted him dead, Mr. Yin,

384
00:23:04,270 --> 00:23:05,290
wouldn't you need only

385
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,220
to step outside?

386
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,620
Then he'd have nowhere to hide.

387
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,940
All I can do now

388
00:23:14,270 --> 00:23:15,220
is stay inside.

389
00:23:16,110 --> 00:23:16,860
As long as I don't go out,

390
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,180
whether he's here

391
00:23:18,350 --> 00:23:19,660
and whether he respects Xinyue Restaurant

392
00:23:21,350 --> 00:23:22,700
can never be proven.

393
00:23:23,590 --> 00:23:25,330
There are some other things

394
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,770
I want to tell you.

395
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,090
In one of the second-floor private rooms

396
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,770
is someone behind Xinyue Restaurant.

397
00:23:34,030 --> 00:23:34,900
Xinyue Restaurant

398
00:23:36,310 --> 00:23:37,860
has someone else behind it?

399
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:39,490
It does.

400
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,980
I can't tell you who.

401
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:46,330
But anyone capable of controlling Xinyue Restaurant from the shadows

402
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:48,380
is no ordinary person.

403
00:23:51,550 --> 00:23:53,420
You do care about your son-in-law, Mr. Yin.

404
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:55,900
Even if I wanted to protect him today,

405
00:23:56,270 --> 00:23:56,940
it'd be difficult.

406
00:23:58,350 --> 00:23:59,090
Miss Huo,

407
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,570
if you can read between the lines,

408
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:03,180
you'll understand what I mean.

409
00:24:06,380 --> 00:24:07,200
[Dong Nianxia]

410
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:08,820
[Daughter of Xiamen's Shipping Magnate]
They may appear graceful and refined,

411
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,690
mysterious and unfathomable,

412
00:24:11,940 --> 00:24:13,880
[Tian Zuocheng, Beiping's Opium King]

413
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,180
crazed and jester-like,

414
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:18,090
[Sun Shaoqin, son of Mr. Yin's friend]
or carefree and unruly,

415
00:24:19,110 --> 00:24:20,940
but these may all be masks.

416
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:23,620
They've come to see whether Xinyue Restaurant's rules

417
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:24,900
still stand

418
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:27,570
and whether I've upheld them well.

419
00:24:28,750 --> 00:24:30,530
If they are displeased,

420
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:32,940
I won't live through the night either.

421
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,730
Tell me. Did you miss me?

422
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:59,620
Don't worry.

423
00:25:00,510 --> 00:25:01,570
My husband

424
00:25:02,070 --> 00:25:04,380
won't appear at Xinyue Restaurant tonight.

425
00:25:08,750 --> 00:25:10,530
Aren't you afraid Mr. Yin will find out?

426
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:12,220
So what if he does?

427
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:15,620
I'm the young mistress of Xinyue Restaurant.

428
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,490
He can't stop me from having an affair.

429
00:25:19,200 --> 00:25:20,490
How many lovers do you need, then?

430
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:26,380
Only you.

431
00:25:28,750 --> 00:25:29,180
Come here.

432
00:25:32,310 --> 00:25:33,330
Come.

433
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,620
I got this for you:

434
00:25:55,750 --> 00:25:58,290
the auction participants' proof-of-funds records.

435
00:26:03,510 --> 00:26:04,830
[Auction Participants' Proof of Funds]
One of them

436
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,330
is someone behind Xinyue Restaurant,

437
00:26:06,680 --> 00:26:07,770
someone even my father wouldn't dare offend.

438
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:16,860
Miss Huo,

439
00:26:18,030 --> 00:26:18,290
sit.

440
00:26:18,590 --> 00:26:19,290
Have something to eat.

441
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:25,980
Here.

442
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:28,250
Try some.

443
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,220
President Tottori, you should know

444
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:39,180
that my condition forbids meat and fish,

445
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,700
especially seafood.

446
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:45,140
Black Plague

447
00:26:46,550 --> 00:26:48,010
is caused by an immune system disorder.

448
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,090
Consuming large amounts of protein

449
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:53,090
can indeed trigger a toxic reaction in the body.

450
00:26:53,590 --> 00:26:54,570
For anyone else,

451
00:26:55,510 --> 00:26:57,140
eating this would be digging their own grave.

452
00:26:59,070 --> 00:27:00,140
But you're different.

453
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:01,700
I have

454
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,220
plenty of medicine.

455
00:27:04,590 --> 00:27:05,620
As long as you

456
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,250
do your job as my adviser at this auction,

457
00:27:09,350 --> 00:27:10,620
you may eat as much as you like.

458
00:27:14,750 --> 00:27:15,180
Here.

459
00:27:15,750 --> 00:27:16,330
Try some.

460
00:27:33,110 --> 00:27:34,420
Thank you, President Tottori.

461
00:27:50,830 --> 00:27:52,180
The late session is about to begin.

462
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:53,420
I should go make preparations.

463
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:53,900
No.

464
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:56,090
I'll send word

465
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:57,490
and have them start later.

466
00:28:03,310 --> 00:28:04,330
All right.

467
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:05,620
I'm only teasing you.

468
00:28:06,550 --> 00:28:07,250
Business comes first.

469
00:28:07,590 --> 00:28:08,220
Go on.

470
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,220
And be very careful.

471
00:28:11,510 --> 00:28:12,460
As soon as the auction ends,

472
00:28:12,750 --> 00:28:13,700
I'll come straight back to you.

473
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,660
What about your deputy chief editor?

474
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:18,140
I'll have to leave him behind.

475
00:28:19,350 --> 00:28:20,220
Then I'll wait here

476
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:22,090
for my Chief Editor Liang

477
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:23,380
to return in triumph.

478
00:28:55,070 --> 00:28:55,620
Stop.

479
00:29:01,310 --> 00:29:02,570
Liang Bencai.

480
00:29:04,070 --> 00:29:05,810
Officer Tottori says he finds you suspicious.

481
00:29:08,070 --> 00:29:09,490
What did you do to offend him?

482
00:29:09,510 --> 00:29:10,290
He sent me to find you.

483
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,490
Yamamoto...

484
00:29:54,880 --> 00:29:55,730
Liang Bencai,

485
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:56,980
you've gone too far!

486
00:29:57,310 --> 00:29:59,250
How dare you bring a drunk into my room?

487
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:01,980
We're through.

488
00:30:02,790 --> 00:30:04,770
You'll never set foot in my room again.

489
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:05,900
Get out!

490
00:30:07,030 --> 00:30:07,730
Miss Yin,

491
00:30:08,030 --> 00:30:09,140
are you all right?

492
00:30:09,270 --> 00:30:10,180
What are you doing here?

493
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:12,420
This is my private affair.

494
00:30:13,110 --> 00:30:14,290
How dare you interfere?

495
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:15,330
Get out!

496
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:16,380
Yes.

497
00:30:43,830 --> 00:30:44,420
What happened?

498
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:45,490
He's dead.

499
00:30:45,830 --> 00:30:48,290
He said Tottori sent him to find Liang Bencai.

500
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:50,380
They must have realized something was wrong with us.

501
00:30:51,310 --> 00:30:51,900
Master Zhang...

502
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:52,860
It was an accident.

503
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,530
Do you think Torii Tottori

504
00:30:58,590 --> 00:30:59,250
has met him before?

505
00:31:00,110 --> 00:31:01,770
Tottori isn't usually stationed in Beiping.

506
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:03,620
It's hard to say.

507
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:09,290
Doesn't this Sasaki

508
00:31:09,830 --> 00:31:11,330
remind you of someone?

509
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,220
President Tottori,

510
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,250
Mr. Sasaki is here.

511
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:27,090
He said you summoned him,

512
00:31:27,830 --> 00:31:28,730
but

513
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:30,770
he's extremely drunk.

514
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:33,250
I simply couldn't reason with him.

515
00:31:34,270 --> 00:31:35,090
Where is he?

516
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:36,700
I'll take you to him.

517
00:31:50,070 --> 00:31:50,490
Sasaki,

518
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:51,530
wake up.

519
00:31:52,830 --> 00:31:53,290
Sasaki?

520
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:55,620
Sasaki,

521
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:56,180
wake up.

522
00:31:56,790 --> 00:31:57,330
This way.

523
00:31:59,000 --> 00:31:59,420
President Tottori.

524
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:14,250
Sasaki!

525
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:29,660
When he wakes, tell him to go back to the garrison

526
00:32:29,790 --> 00:32:31,050
to report for punishment.

527
00:32:31,830 --> 00:32:32,180
Yes.

528
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:18,770
Let go!

529
00:33:19,110 --> 00:33:20,220
Let go, you fool!

530
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:22,220
Let go!

531
00:33:22,790 --> 00:33:23,620
Let go!

532
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,220
My apologies.

533
00:33:26,270 --> 00:33:26,730
Forgive his behavior.

534
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:29,490
What a disgrace to the Empire of Japan!

535
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:32,730
I'm sorry.

536
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:43,090
He's gone.

537
00:33:45,310 --> 00:33:45,860
Gone?

538
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:56,460
What a waste of such good wine.

539
00:34:11,570 --> 00:34:12,980
They do look somewhat alike.

540
00:34:13,230 --> 00:34:15,380
No wonder Chen Pi always gets on my nerves.

541
00:34:20,630 --> 00:34:22,900
A great many unexpected things

542
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:25,530
have happened during this one-hour intermission.

543
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:27,260
Did you notice

544
00:34:27,590 --> 00:34:29,460
anyone unusual in the private rooms?

545
00:34:29,460 --> 00:34:30,590
[Private Room Three]

546
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:32,340
I'm Chen Minzhi

547
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:33,530
of Yahe Monthly.

548
00:34:34,400 --> 00:34:35,340
Sorry to disturb you.

549
00:34:42,150 --> 00:34:43,380
It's you?

550
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:47,340
I never expected

551
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:49,380
to meet an old acquaintance here.

552
00:35:04,280 --> 00:35:05,380
I just took my medicine.

553
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:08,740
What happened earlier

554
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:10,860
put me somewhat on edge.

555
00:35:12,070 --> 00:35:13,210
I'll be fine soon.

556
00:35:15,030 --> 00:35:17,170
Can you really not quit morphine?

557
00:35:19,110 --> 00:35:19,900
Without it,

558
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:22,530
I can't think.

559
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:26,420
You should get some rest.

560
00:35:55,510 --> 00:35:56,380
Gentlemen,

561
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:58,980
you won only one lot in the early session.

562
00:35:59,230 --> 00:36:00,650
According to Xinyue Restaurant's rules,

563
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:02,820
you cannot participate in the late session.

564
00:36:02,880 --> 00:36:03,530
What?

565
00:36:04,670 --> 00:36:06,420
We can't enter the late session after winning only one lot?

566
00:36:06,420 --> 00:36:07,570
Who made such an absurd rule?

567
00:36:08,070 --> 00:36:09,740
None of you ever told us about it.

568
00:36:11,030 --> 00:36:12,570
My boss paid a fortune

569
00:36:12,590 --> 00:36:13,610
for this private room.

570
00:36:13,840 --> 00:36:15,210
We were promised it for the entire auction.

571
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:17,050
Now you're throwing us out halfway through?

572
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:18,530
How is that fair?

573
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:20,340
Look at this.

574
00:36:20,590 --> 00:36:22,090
We saved all this money

575
00:36:22,190 --> 00:36:23,170
for the late session.

576
00:36:23,230 --> 00:36:24,260
Please don't be angry.

577
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:25,380
I haven't finished.

578
00:36:26,190 --> 00:36:27,940
You're honored guests from the early session

579
00:36:28,190 --> 00:36:29,010
who paid a substantial sum.

580
00:36:29,550 --> 00:36:32,130
You may move to the main hall

581
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:34,570
and continue watching the late session,

582
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:36,980
but you may no longer bid.

583
00:36:37,110 --> 00:36:38,820
Are you humiliating my boss?

584
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,780
You're throwing us out of here?

585
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:42,490
My boss can't afford such disgrace.

586
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,860
We're not going.

587
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:48,210
We came here to make a name for ourselves.

588
00:36:48,590 --> 00:36:50,980
A seat in some corner downstairs

589
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:52,980
might be acceptable.

590
00:36:53,440 --> 00:36:54,380
- But... - Gentlemen,

591
00:36:54,670 --> 00:36:55,650
my sincere apologies.

592
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:56,780
I'll arrange it at once.

593
00:37:12,760 --> 00:37:13,780
Give the guests from Private Room Six

594
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:14,940
a conspicuous table.

595
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:16,420
We don't know who they are.

596
00:37:16,630 --> 00:37:17,650
If they're out of sight,

597
00:37:18,030 --> 00:37:18,980
there may be trouble.

598
00:37:39,230 --> 00:37:40,090
Ladies and gentlemen,

599
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:44,130
the late session will now officially begin.

600
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:47,900
There are ten lots in this session,

601
00:37:48,190 --> 00:37:49,820
[Featured Highlights]
all exceptional treasures.

602
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:52,300
The minimum bid increment

603
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,900
is 10,000 silver coins,

604
00:37:54,190 --> 00:37:55,820
with no upper limit.

605
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:01,170
Our first lot is a Han dynasty

606
00:38:02,110 --> 00:38:03,940
recumbent jade ram.

607
00:38:14,190 --> 00:38:14,900
Ladies and gentlemen,

608
00:38:15,590 --> 00:38:17,460
bidding begins now.

609
00:38:18,030 --> 00:38:18,650
Fifty thousand.

610
00:38:19,150 --> 00:38:21,210
Table 11 bids 50,000.

611
00:38:22,710 --> 00:38:23,380
Sixty thousand.

612
00:38:23,670 --> 00:38:25,340
Table 10 bids 60,000.

613
00:38:25,510 --> 00:38:26,170
Eighty thousand.

614
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,740
Private Room Seven bids 80,000.

615
00:38:29,230 --> 00:38:29,940
One hundred and ten thousand.

616
00:38:30,110 --> 00:38:32,090
Table 14 bids 110,000.

617
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,050
One hundred and twenty thousand.

618
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:34,130
One hundred and fifty thousand!

619
00:38:34,550 --> 00:38:35,260
Two hundred thousand!

620
00:38:39,180 --> 00:38:45,180
[Magical Artifact Chests]

621
00:39:01,740 --> 00:39:05,900
♪The past fades like smoke♪

622
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,980
♪A choice is made in silence♪

623
00:39:09,260 --> 00:39:12,060
♪In this labyrinthine puzzle♪

624
00:39:12,460 --> 00:39:16,220
♪Who can reach the shore?♪

625
00:39:16,460 --> 00:39:19,900
♪Just an ordinary farewell♪

626
00:39:20,180 --> 00:39:23,580
♪The sun seems to shine bright over our heads♪

627
00:39:23,660 --> 00:39:30,940
♪But this could be our last trip together♪

628
00:39:31,380 --> 00:39:34,660
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

629
00:39:34,940 --> 00:39:38,180
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

630
00:39:38,340 --> 00:39:42,380
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

631
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:45,940
♪Who believes in fate?♪

632
00:39:46,180 --> 00:39:49,540
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

633
00:39:49,780 --> 00:39:53,060
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

634
00:39:53,380 --> 00:39:57,060
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

635
00:39:57,260 --> 00:40:00,500
♪Take care♪

636
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:03,060
♪We once raced♪

637
00:40:03,140 --> 00:40:05,060
♪For the dawn♪

638
00:40:05,220 --> 00:40:08,500
♪Ever-lasting bond, a satisfying vindication♪

639
00:40:08,620 --> 00:40:11,900
♪In the web of fate♪

640
00:40:11,900 --> 00:40:15,100
♪No one can escape♪

641
00:40:16,100 --> 00:40:17,940
♪Life and death cut like a blade♪

642
00:40:18,100 --> 00:40:19,660
♪We too were young once♪

643
00:40:19,740 --> 00:40:23,180
♪Fortunate to brave the raging waves together♪

644
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:25,700
♪Keep the ember lit♪

645
00:40:25,820 --> 00:40:30,340
♪To illuminate the journey ahead♪

646
00:40:30,460 --> 00:40:33,420
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

647
00:40:33,660 --> 00:40:37,180
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

648
00:40:37,300 --> 00:40:41,060
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

649
00:40:41,380 --> 00:40:44,860
♪Who believes in fate?♪

650
00:40:45,020 --> 00:40:48,020
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

651
00:40:48,260 --> 00:40:52,020
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

652
00:40:52,180 --> 00:40:55,900
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

653
00:40:56,020 --> 00:41:07,460
♪Please, do take care of yourself♪
